  "reason": "The records collectively make the later result plausibly reconstructible. R1 and R19 directly establish SPS at 1000 °C for mechanically alloyed, compositionally similar transition-metal HEAs, while R17 shows that approximately 1000–1050 °C SPS can produce a dense microstructure without substantial coarsening. R3, R10, R13, R16, and R20 show that SPS of milled BCC HEA powders can generate distributed oxide or secondary phases through temperature-activated diffusion. Most importantly, R2, R4, R6, R9, R11, R13, and R14 connect dense, continuous oxide/passive films with suppressed oxygen or ion penetration, and R13 explicitly links higher SPS temperature and diffusion to improved passivation. An expert could therefore combine the demonstrated 1000 °C SPS treatment with oxide precipitation and dense-film barrier mechanisms to propose the later intervention and its corrosion/oxidation rationale, although the exact MgAlTiVFeCo oxide assemblage and numerical optimum would still require experiment."
